{{!-- v3 Bio tab.

      FOURTH PART MIGRATED. 123 lines on v2, four inline styles, ten `autofocus` and ten `required`,
      and — for nine of the thirteen splats — almost nothing in it.

      WHAT THE CENSUS SAYS THIS TAB IS, WHICH IS NOT WHAT IT LOOKS LIKE
      -----------------------------------------------------------------
      Only FOUR splats declare bio splatfields at all (`assets/data/sheet/biotab.js`, counted
      2026-08-04: vampire 6, werewolf 5, mage 7, wraith 7). `mortal` declares `{}` and eight declare
      nothing. So for nine of thirteen this tab is a portrait, a name, four generic fields and two
      prose boxes — which is why the layout below must look deliberate when it is nearly empty, not
      merely un-full. Two consequences are designed in rather than discovered later:

        * the identity row is a WRAPPING FLEX ROW, not a three-column grid. A grid reserves its
          third track whether or not anything lands in it; a flex row simply has two children.
        * the splatfield column is REMOVED, not merely emptied, when the partial produced no field
          — see `.v3-biosplat` in css/pc-actor-v3.css. The alternative is a 320px hole on nine
          splats, and 320px is an INLINE width inside a shared partial, so it cannot be un-set from
          a stylesheet (D4: inline styles beat author rules, and there is no `[style]` sledgehammer
          in this project).

      THE PROSE, WHICH IS THE ACTUAL PROBLEM ON THIS TAB
      -------------------------------------------------
      A mage carries roughly 7,000 characters across three splatfield textboxes (paradigma ~1,000,
      práctica ~3,500, instrumentos ~2,500); a wraith has four (life, death, regret, thorns). No
      other splat declares a textbox at all. On v2 those render as undifferentiated stacked blocks,
      each with `min-height: 150px` (`.textarea`, wod.css:556) and no upper bound — a wall.

      Long ones are therefore wrapped in a native `<details>` when the sheet is LOCKED. Three things
      about that choice, each of which is a compromise stated out loud rather than papered over:

      1. IT IS DISCLOSURE, NOT A CLAMP. `<details>` hides its content; it cannot show the first six
         lines of it. A real clamp needs either a duplicated preview (the same 3,500 characters in
         the DOM twice, and a `<summary>` whose accessible NAME would be that whole text) or the
         prose inside the `<summary>`, which is invalid content and announces catastrophically. So
         the threshold below exists to make disclosure behave like a clamp where it matters: a field
         SHORTER than `CLAMP_AT` characters is never hidden, because hiding an 80-character paradigm
         behind a click is a regression, and a field longer than it is worth one click.

      2. IT DOES NOT PERSIST, and it resets on every re-render, not merely on reopen. The store that
         would persist it (`game.user.flags.wod[<actorId>]`, driven by `_handleUnfoldClick` /
         `_restoreUnfoldState`) is reachable only by reproducing an exact DOM shape: the handler
         walks `parentElement` three times and toggles `.hide`/`.show` on that ancestor's SIBLINGS by
         class name. Satisfying it here would have meant one wrapper `<div>` that exists for no
         reason but the walk, plus a marker element whose only job is to receive a class (because
         `.hide` is `display: none !important`, wod.css:609, so the class cannot be repurposed to
         mean "clamped" without spending the `!important` budget on it). That is not reuse, it is a
         shape-dependency on machinery the design already records as fragile — so `<details>` it is,
         per the brief's own fallback. It buys back native keyboard operability and a real
         `aria-expanded`, which the v2 unfold `<i>` has never had.

      3. IT APPLIES TO SPLATFIELD TEXTBOXES ONLY. Appearance, Biography and the GM tips render open,
         exactly as on v2. They are the only prose the other nine splats have, and collapsing the
         sole content of a nearly-empty tab is the opposite of the fix.

      SHELL/ROW SPLIT (add-pc-sheet-v3 D5), AND THE ONE PLACE IT BENDS
      ---------------------------------------------------------------
      Every `data-action` below (`editImage`) and every `data-*` is one `parts/bio.hbs` already
      emits, carried across unchanged; nothing is added and nothing is dropped. `bio_splatfields.hbs`
      is still INCLUDED, untouched — it is a row renderer (a per-field loop carrying the
      `generationChange` controls) and forking it is exactly what D5 forbids.

      `bio_splatboxes.hbs` is NOT included, and this is the bend. That partial is nine lines: an
      `{{#each splatfields}}`, a `type == "textbox"` test, and one `{{> description.hbs}}`. To wrap
      each textbox in its own `<details>` the wrapper has to be INSIDE that loop, so the loop is
      reproduced here. What is duplicated is three lines of iteration; the row renderer itself
      (`description.hbs`) is still the shared one, called with the same six arguments in the same
      order. `bio_splatboxes.hbs` stays registered and is what the v2 sheet still renders.

      TWO DEFECTS FIXED, NEITHER OF THEM COSMETIC
      -------------------------------------------
      * `required` and `autofocus` are GONE (ten of each on v2). `required` was never a validation
        intent: it is the CSS hook `.floating-label-group input:not(:focus):valid ~ .floating-label`
        needs (wod.css:1001-1029), so every EMPTY bio field on v2 is `:invalid` and announces to
        assistive technology as an invalid form field — on a sheet where every one of these fields is
        genuinely optional. `autofocus` is undefined behaviour past the first instance and steals
        focus on open. A real `<label>` wrapping its input needs neither, and needs no `id` either:
        two PC sheets can be open at once and a duplicated `id` binds both labels to one input.
        `name`, `type` and `data-dtype` are carried across exactly — that is what the submit path
        reads, and v2's bio inputs carry no `data-name` at all, so none is added here.

        THREE `autofocus` AND THREE `required` SURVIVE, in `bio_splatfields.hbs:12,14,23`. They
        cannot be removed from here: it is a shared partial and editing it changes the v2 sheet.

      * LOCKED FIELDS ARE `readonly`, not merely nameless. v2 renders a locked field as an ordinary
        editable `<input>` with no `name` attribute — it takes focus, accepts typing, and throws the
        value away on submit because nothing names it. `readonly` + `aria-readonly` says so to the
        user and to assistive technology. --}}
<section class="tab {{tab.cssClass}}" data-tab="{{tab.id}}" data-group="{{tab.group}}" data-drop-area="true">

	<div class="v3-tabhead">
		{{!-- No create control, deliberately: the v2 Bio tab authors nothing, and D5 forbids v3
		      emitting a `data-action` its counterpart lacks. The header is title-only. --}}
		<h2 class="v3-tabtitle splatFont">{{localize "wod.tab.bio"}}</h2>
	</div>

	<div class="v3-tabbody">
		<div class="v3-tabmain">

			{{!-- The identity row. On v2 this is `<div style="display: flex">` holding a
			      `style="flex: 1; margin-left: auto"` portrait, a `style="width: 320px"` field column
			      and a second `style="width: 320px"` column inside the splatfields partial — three of
			      the tab's four inline styles. Two of them are removed here; the third belongs to the
			      shared partial and is neutralised by making its parent a flex container, where a
			      `width` becomes a flex BASIS that shrinks instead of a floor that overflows. --}}
			<div class="v3-section v3-bioidentity">

				<div class="v3-portrait">
					{{#if locked}}
						<img class="profile-img {{#if (eq actor.img 'icons/svg/mystery-man.svg')}}defaultimage{{/if}}" src="{{actor.img}}" alt="{{actor.name}}" />
					{{else}}
						{{#if userpermissions.changeActorImage}}
							{{!-- `data-action="editImage"` + `data-edit="img"` is the ONLY in-sheet route to
							      changing a PC's portrait (`OnEditImage`, action-helpers.js), so it travels
							      with the tab exactly as authored. `pointer` is v2's cursor class and is kept
							      because the control is genuinely clickable here. --}}
							<img class="profile-img {{#if (eq actor.img 'icons/svg/mystery-man.svg')}}defaultimage{{/if}} pointer" src="{{actor.img}}" title="{{actor.name}}" alt="{{actor.name}}" data-action="editImage" data-edit="img" />
						{{else}}
							<img class="profile-img {{#if (eq actor.img 'icons/svg/mystery-man.svg')}}defaultimage{{/if}}" src="{{actor.img}}" alt="{{actor.name}}" />
						{{/if}}
					{{/if}}
				</div>

				<div class="v3-biocore">
					<div class="v3-fields">
						<label class="v3-field">
							<span class="v3-fieldlabel">{{localize 'wod.bio.name'}}</span>
							{{#if locked}}
								<input class="sheet-infoValues" type="text" value="{{actor.name}}" autocomplete="off" readonly aria-readonly="true" />
							{{else}}
								<input class="sheet-infoValues editable" name="name" type="text" value="{{actor.name}}" data-dtype="String" autocomplete="off" />
							{{/if}}
						</label>

						{{!-- Nature and Demeanour are a changeling's Legacies instead, declared in that
						      splat's own field set, so v2 suppresses the generic pair for changelings. Both
						      gates are carried across verbatim, including the `mini` permission level, which
						      is a GM setting rather than a splat property. --}}
						{{#if (ne actor.system.settings.splat config.splat.changeling)}}
							{{#if (ne (checkSystemsetting "viewBiotabPermission") "mini")}}
								<label class="v3-field">
									<span class="v3-fieldlabel">{{localize 'wod.bio.nature'}}</span>
									{{#if locked}}
										<input class="sheet-infoValues" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.nature}}" autocomplete="off" readonly aria-readonly="true" />
									{{else}}
										<input class="sheet-infoValues editable" name="system.bio.nature" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.nature}}" data-dtype="String" autocomplete="off" />
									{{/if}}
								</label>
							{{/if}}

							<label class="v3-field">
								<span class="v3-fieldlabel">{{localize 'wod.bio.demeanor'}}</span>
								{{#if locked}}
									<input class="sheet-infoValues" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.demeanor}}" autocomplete="off" readonly aria-readonly="true" />
								{{else}}
									<input class="sheet-infoValues editable" name="system.bio.demeanor" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.demeanor}}" data-dtype="String" autocomplete="off" />
								{{/if}}
							</label>
						{{/if}}

						{{#if (ne (checkSystemsetting "viewBiotabPermission") "mini")}}
							<label class="v3-field">
								<span class="v3-fieldlabel">{{localize 'wod.bio.concept'}}</span>
								{{#if locked}}
									<input class="sheet-infoValues" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.concept}}" autocomplete="off" readonly aria-readonly="true" />
								{{else}}
									<input class="sheet-infoValues editable" name="system.bio.concept" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.concept}}" data-dtype="String" autocomplete="off" />
								{{/if}}
							</label>

							<label class="v3-field">
								<span class="v3-fieldlabel">{{localize 'wod.bio.derangement'}}</span>
								{{#if locked}}
									<input class="sheet-infoValues" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.derangement}}" autocomplete="off" readonly aria-readonly="true" />
								{{else}}
									<input class="sheet-infoValues editable" name="system.bio.derangement" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.derangement}}" data-dtype="String" autocomplete="off" />
								{{/if}}
							</label>
						{{/if}}
					</div>
				</div>

				{{!-- The splat's own identity fields, from the SHARED partial, with its arguments
				      unchanged. This wrapper exists so the stylesheet has something to hold on to: it
				      makes the partial's inline 320px a shrinkable flex basis, and it is what
				      disappears when the partial produced no field at all. --}}
				<div class="v3-biosplat">
					{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/bio_splatfields.hbs" locked=locked}}
				</div>

			</div>

			{{!-- The splatfield prose. `bio_splatboxes.hbs`'s loop, reproduced so that each box can be
			      wrapped individually — see the header for why that is the one duplication here, and
			      why it is three lines of iteration rather than a row renderer.

			      CLAMP_AT = 600. Measured on the STORED HTML string, tags included, so it is a
			      deliberately generous heuristic rather than a character count of the prose: a mage's
			      three fields are ~1,000 / ~3,500 / ~2,500 and clear it easily, while a one-paragraph
			      answer does not and is never hidden. A field that sits just over the line loses one
			      click and nothing else, which is why the threshold does not need to be exact. --}}
			{{#each splatfields as |field key|}}
				{{#if (eq field.type "textbox")}}
					<div class="v3-section">
						{{#if ../locked}}
							{{#if (gt field.value.length 600)}}
								<details class="v3-prose">
									<summary class="v3-prosesummary">
										{{!-- `fa-angles-right`, rotated by CSS when open. The same glyph the XP
										      ledgers use for exactly this idea, so the sheet keeps one
										      vocabulary for "there is more here"; `aria-hidden` because
										      `<summary>` already carries the expanded state natively. --}}
										<i class="fa-solid fa-angles-right v3-prosechevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
										<span class="v3-proselabel splatFont">{{localize field.label}}</span>
									</summary>
									<div class="v3-prosebody">
										{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/description.hbs" proseheadline=field.label locked=../locked headline=false prosename=(concat "system.bio.splatfields." key ".value") prosevalue=field.value proseenriched=field.enriched}}
									</div>
								</details>
							{{else}}
								{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/description.hbs" proseheadline=field.label locked=../locked headline=false prosename=(concat "system.bio.splatfields." key ".value") prosevalue=field.value proseenriched=field.enriched}}
							{{/if}}
						{{else}}
							{{!-- Unlocked: a prose-mirror editor, never wrapped. Collapsing an editor hides
							      the thing the user opened the sheet to change. --}}
							{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/description.hbs" proseheadline=field.label locked=../locked headline=false prosename=(concat "system.bio.splatfields." key ".value") prosevalue=field.value proseenriched=field.enriched}}
						{{/if}}
					</div>
				{{/if}}
			{{/each}}

			{{#if graphicsettings.useLinkPlatform}}
				<div class="v3-section">
					<h3 class="v3-sectiontitle splatFont">{{localize 'wod.bio.worldanvil'}}</h3>

					{{#if locked}}
						<p class="v3-linkline">
							{{#if (ne actor.system.bio.worldanvil "")}}
								<a href="{{actor.system.bio.worldanvil}}" target="_blank">{{localize 'wod.bio.worldanvillink'}}</a>
							{{else}}
								{{localize 'wod.bio.noworldanvillink'}}
							{{/if}}
						</p>
					{{else}}
						{{!-- v2 sized this with `style="width: 90%"`. A labelled field in the grid needs no
						      width at all, and the `{{#if (eq locked false)}}editable{{/if}}` it carried was
						      unconditional — this branch only exists when unlocked. --}}
						<div class="v3-fields">
							<label class="v3-field">
								<span class="v3-fieldlabel">{{localize 'wod.bio.worldanvil'}}</span>
								<input class="sheet-infoValues editable" name="system.bio.worldanvil" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.worldanvil}}" data-dtype="String" autocomplete="off" />
							</label>
						</div>
					{{/if}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{!-- The three generic prose boxes, open, exactly as v2 renders them. `headline=false` is
			      v2's argument and is kept: `description.hbs` draws its own heading either way, and the
			      flag only picks which of the two heading classes it uses. --}}
			<div class="v3-section">
				{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/description.hbs" proseheadline="wod.bio.appearance" locked=locked headline=false prosename="system.bio.appearance" prosevalue=appearance proseenriched=enrichedAppearance}}
			</div>

			{{#if (ne (checkSystemsetting "viewBiotabPermission") "mini")}}
				<div class="v3-section">
					{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/description.hbs" proseheadline="wod.bio.background" locked=locked headline=false prosename="system.bio.background" prosevalue=background proseenriched=enrichedBackground}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{#if isGM}}
				<div class="v3-section">
					{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/description.hbs" proseheadline="wod.bio.tips" locked=locked headline=false prosename="system.bio.roleplaytip" prosevalue=roleplaytip proseenriched=enrichedRoleplaytip}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

		</div>

		<aside class="v3-macrorail">
			{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/macro_icons.hbs"}}
		</aside>
	</div>

</section>
